---
// Going between Home and About without a full page load, so that the topic map, at the same place on both pages, is
// moved rather than drawn again, and the background with it. Layout renders this in the <head> of the pages that have
// the intro and its map (its introMap prop). It is Astro's ClientRouter, held to those pages:
// - A link between them swaps the page in place. TopicMap carries its canvas over to the next page's map, and
//   Background keeps its element (data-astro-transition-persist); everything else is the next page's own.
// - A link from them to any other page loads it in full, as before, without the router fetching it first. Pages
//   without this component load in full anyway.
// - The page changes at once, as in the prototype: no cross-fade, and a plain swap where view transitions are missing.
// - Nothing is prefetched (prefetch: false in astro.config.mjs), as before.
//
// A page's own script runs once, the first time the page is shown, and stays: a listener it adds to document or
// window also hears the other page's events, and anything it found in the page is gone once the router swaps it.
import { ClientRouter } from 'astro:transitions';
---

<ClientRouter fallback="swap" />

<script>
	// Home and About, the pages that share the map. Any other page, even one with this component, loads in full.
	const INTRO_PAGES = new Set(['/', '/about/']);

	document.addEventListener('astro:before-preparation', (event) => {
		if (!INTRO_PAGES.has(event.to.pathname)) event.preventDefault();
	});
</script>

{/* Astro's transition:animate="none", for the whole page. Inline, so that only these pages have it. */}
<style is:inline>
	::view-transition-group(root) { animation: none; }
	::view-transition-old(root) { animation: none; opacity: 0; mix-blend-mode: normal; }
	::view-transition-new(root) { animation: none; mix-blend-mode: normal; }
</style>
